A||||12||MooCow||How relaible is the 4:10 4-speed trannies??||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||09-24-2001||01:50 AM||||As nearly all of you know my tranny died and I get another one but am unsure about reliability.  I only have driven the car about 6,000 and the trans cracked on me.  Should I just save my money and get a <BR>5-speed??  I truly do love my 4-speed but am unsure about it being reliable now.<BR>All input would be great.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-24-2001||02:11 AM||||The trannys are reliable, but take a look at the case...I believe the 84s cases are weaker than the 85+ because there is no additional webbing on the case(unless the 4.10s do have the webbing-don't remember)  The cases are smooth--nicer looking, but weaker.<P>Take the internals from the 4.10 and put them in a newer case and you'll have a nice strong trans.<P>What exactly broke on you?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">    <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jefrysuko||09-24-2001||11:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>I believe the 84s cases are weaker than the 85+ because there is no additional webbing on the case(unless the 4.10s do have the webbing-don't remember)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think you might have that backwards.  I was told by Rodney once that the 4.10 was strongest case that was ever put in a fiero.  You might want to check with him though to make sure I understood right.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-24-2001||11:33 AM||||I have also heard that the 4.10 case (actually, I think all the 84 cases) were weaker. I think they were beefed up in 85 to handle the V-6. You could probably find an 85 or later 4-speed pretty cheap. Someone who knows what they're doing could put your 4.10 ring and pinion in the later model tranny.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jaei Sun||09-24-2001||01:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Should I just save my money and get a <BR>5-speed?? I truly do love my 4-speed but am unsure about it being reliable now.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WTH... wern't you the one saying how much you hate shifting... and how you were going to trade your car (with a fresh 3.4 and a new paint job) for a different fiero with an auto?  And now you're saying you love your 4-speed.  Hey why don't you get an auto since that's what you wanted.||||reg||3
Z||000005||FieroMaster88||09-24-2001||01:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B> WTH... wern't you the one saying how much you hate shifting... and how you were going to trade your car (with a fresh 3.4 and a new paint job) for a different fiero with an auto?  And now you're saying you love your 4-speed.  Hey why don't you get an auto since that's what you wanted.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>He is not gonna get an auto because he finally realised how fast his car is with the 4 speed...and now he likes it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Amazing huh? <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||09-24-2001||01:50 PM||||I liked the 4spd in my 86 SEV6 the best. Five speeds always sound better, but in everyday use....I liked the 4spd better. <BR>I liked where reverse was too. <P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||MooCow||09-24-2001||03:07 PM||||Yea after driving an auto finally and them my stick it was far better.  I love my stick now.  The only real reason I hated the stick was of fear of killing the clutch but not anymore.  Ed Parks just told me that what happened to my 4:10 was very rare.  He has had his in his for a long time and it is still holding up.  I think I may just wait till next year and then decide cause college is now starting for me and I really dont have time to mess with it all that much.  We will see what happens.  I am just trying to get the better of the 2 trannies for my 3.4.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||09-24-2001||04:34 PM||||Well, if you go to a 5-speed, you'll loose that 4.10 gearing off the line, but you'll gain an OD for cruising.  It's a trade off, depending on whether or not you do much highway cruising.  <P>If you're gonna wait until next year to decide, why don't you just JBWeld the case up and drive it as is for a while.  The only thing you could hurt would be the tranny, which you're gonna replace anyway.||||reg||6
Z||000009||Tina||09-24-2001||07:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> I truly do love my 4-speed [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, there's your answer Ken.<BR>The only other suggestion I got for you,is<BR>to see if a fellow Fiero nut let's you drive<BR>a 5-speed for gear ratio comparison.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW How many miles did yours have?||||reg||1
Z||000010||jelly2m8||09-24-2001||08:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>The trannys are reliable, but take a look at the case...I believe the 84s cases are weaker than the 85+ because there is no additional webbing on the case(unless the 4.10s do have the webbing-don't remember)  The cases are smooth--nicer looking, but weaker.<P>Take the internals from the 4.10 and put them in a newer case and you'll have a nice strong trans.<P>What exactly broke on you?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 84 internals MAY NOT fit in the 85-86 4 spd case.<P> I haven't tried to put 84 internals in a 85-86 case, but I have tried to put a set of 85 gear sets in a 84 case. The case internals ( shape) were slightly different, and the 1st-2nd shift fork was interfering with the input and output shaft bearing bosses. I had to dig out a 85 case to put the gear sets in.<P>Having said this I just looked at the P22, and it shows the cases as having the same part numbers. So again I state it MAY NOT work.<P> I have run a 84 4.10 4 spd behind my V8, and used it hard enough to spin a rod bearing, but the tranny held up perfectly.<P> If you pull the case apart, check around the differental assembly, a common problem is that the differental  pin will break, resulting in either the differental pin and or the differental / side gears go flying around in the case, sometimes they will go through the bottom.  The biggest cause of this is spinning the tires, as usually only 1 tire spins resulting in the differental gears putting a heavy load on the differental pin. This puts extreme wear on the differental pin, usually resulting in failure.||||reg||1
Z||000011||MooCow||09-25-2001||12:09 AM||||Well after talking to Ed about the whole thing I think I am going to stick with my 4:10.  He had the 4:10 in his white coupe then put in an Isuzu and now has gone back to the 4:10 because it is faster off the line and is more relialbe than the Isuzus.   He told me he has only ever seen about 6 4:10 speeds ever break.  So since my setup is already for the 4:10 and since I truly do love the 4:10 I think I am going to stick with it.  Also I do not really go on the highway that much except for car shows and on the highway I kinda like the higher RPM's.  As far as fixing this one I highly doubt it.<BR>Tina I have driven in both 5-speeds and I like the Isuzu better but is still nothing like the 4:10.  Thanks everyone for there input.  Now I just have to get the tranny in and decide if I want to drive it at all this year or just wait till next year.<P>Thanks again,  Ken||||reg||10
Z||000012||1FST2M6||09-25-2001||08:37 AM||||i broke clutches, and wiped out rod bearings, and was running nitrous through mine.. GT Bastard is still railing on it.  you just got a bad seed. ||||reg||1
